    "reason": "the library estimator named 'Beaufort-style' is a Ridge(alpha=1.0) on seven individual air lags plus two harmonics fitted over the whole year; the cited method is an OLS regression on a single right-aligned 2-10 d moving average of air temperature, selected per station by R2, fitted on summer days only. A faithful reimplementation now exists and is scored here on the identical cases.",
